<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.7.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02192</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.7.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3b81dcac-bc14-4992-9f26-2993e200c421</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><emphasis><emphasis>
    <para>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
  </emphasis></emphasis>
<para>For questions 1 – 7, find the factored form of the quadratic expression.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+4x − 12\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 2)(x − 6)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 3)(x − 4)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 2)(x − 6)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 2)(x + 6)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 2)(x + 6)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−3x −18\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 9)(x + 2)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 6)(x + 3)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 18)(x + 1)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 7)(x + 3)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 6)(x + 3)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2− 12x − 45\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 45)(x + 1)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 8)(x − 4)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 9)(x + 5)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 15)(x + 3)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 15)(x + 3)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−x −20\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 10)(x + 2)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 5)(x + 4)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 20)(x + 1)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 5)(x − 4)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 5)(x + 4)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+2x −35\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 5)(x + 7)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 5)(x + 7)\) </item>
  <item> \((x + 5)(x − 7)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 5)(x − 7)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 5)(x + 7)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−23x −50\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 10)(x + 5)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 50)(x + 1)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 25)(x + 2)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 10)(x − 13)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 25)(x + 2)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+7x −60\)</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \((x − 5)(x + 12)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 20)(x + 3)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 10)(x + 3)\) </item>
  <item> \((x − 4)(x + 15)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((x − 5)(x + 12)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Consider the expression \(x^2+bx −80\), where the leading coefficient equals 1. Identify all the pairs of factors of –80 that would result in positive values of \(b\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 80 and 1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>–80 and 1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>–80 and –1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 80 and –1,</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 80 and –1, 40 and –2, 20 and –4, 16 and –5, 10 and –8</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Consider the expression \(x^2+ bx − 80\), where the leading coefficient equals 1. Identify all the pairs of factors of –80 that would result in negative values of \(b\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 80 and 1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>–80 and 1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>–80 and –1,</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 80 and –1,</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –80 and 1, –40 and 2, –20 and 4, –16 and 5, –10 and 8</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Here are pairs of equivalent expressions: one in standard form and the other in factored form. Identify the missing symbols:</item>
</list>
<para>\(x^2\; \square \; 15x \;\square\; 34\) and \((x + 2)(x − 17)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> − and − </item>
  <item> + and − </item>
  <item> + and + </item>
  <item> − and + </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> − and −</para></section>
</content>
</document>
